what do I think about the try-hard  mentality I'm gonna answer that question  in today's episode of ask Evan so I got  a question for one of my youtube viewers  love you guys rui goooo who wrote in to  say hey Evan what are your thoughts on  the try-hard mentality so I'm not super  familiar with the try-hard mentality my  understanding of it is it's when you're  working really hard on something but  you're not seeing results it's kind of  like busywork you're working just to  work and you're not actually moving  forward on anything that you're doing  and so if that's what you're doing it's  not good but for any big goal that you  have you have to work really hard right  it's not just working smart it's working  smart and working hard and you have to  try really hard to make that happen and  I like to think of it in terms of not  having regrets in my life and feeling  like I gave everything I had to whatever  project I was working on i'ma give you  an example something that's happening  right now I'm in the process of  acquiring a business and as part of that  process I want to bring on a team leader  to help run a good chunk of the company  and at first he said no and I went home  and thought about I think well maybe  there's got to be another way to do it  you know I wanted to make sure that  every stone was was was turned over  every possible opportunity every  possible angle was explored I didn't  want to feel like there was some other  way that we could structure this deal to  make it work so he would say yes and so  you know two nights ago is up until five  in the morning structuring a deal we met  again last night and he was here at my  place until midnight working on another  deal and and it looks like we have  something in place you know maybe next  week i have a video to update you guys  and what's happening but it was all of  that work was because  you know even though he said no to start  I wanted to make sure just in my own  head that I I explored every single  angle every possible way to accomplish  my goal I tried and if he at the end of  that said no that's cool I would move on  and find somebody else and I get  somebody else to kind of run that  position but I didn't want to live the  rest of my life in regret thinking like  man what if I just tried this angle of  that angle or this angle right and  hoping that maybe that would have worked  out and so if you have a dream a lot of  times the most logical path or the path  that you think is going to work out  doesn't and so if you want to hit that  dream you've got to take detours you've  got to find other ways of saying you got  to take a different way to get there and  that comes from trying hard and doing a  lot of work to do it my second quick  thought on it is you want to do things  out of passion and you're not working  hard just to look like you're busy you  know make everybody look at you and say  well that guy's doing a ton of work but  you're you're working as a byproduct of  you being excited about something but  you've been passionate about something  when you love doing something it almost  doesn't feel like you're doing work  because you're still engrossed in it and  you have such a commitment level to it  and so I would focus not on how much  work you're doing but are you doing work  that you love because if you're doing  work that you love you're going to try  hard and do a good job of it and put in  the hours that you need to be successful  if you look at any successful  entrepreneur and track their growth it  came from putting in insane amounts of  hours working smart plus working hard  doing something that they love and so  those are my quick thoughts hopefully an  answer the question and continue to  believe so I'd love to know from you  guys what do you think about the try  hard mentality leave it in the comments  below I'm going to join in the  discussion thank you so much for  watching continue to believe and I'll  see you soon
 

